0019: per-pixel shadow pass (real-time GI work package XR-06). Client exports RemixBridge_GiPixelOpen, RemixBridge_GiPixelPass and RemixBridge_GiPixelReadCounters. The server asks its renderer for DXVK's ID3D9VkExternalPass (native/dxvk patch 0004) and ray queries (0003); with both, a pass records a ray-query compute kernel into the renderer's command stream: the top level is built from the capsules and boxes of the block the client sends, the kernel samples the INTZ depth texture and writes four quarter-resolution outputs, which are copied into the client's A16B16G16R16F render target textures. Stream order makes a draw sent after the pass sample its outputs; nothing waits. A stock renderer or a device without ray queries answers the open with an off state and the reason in the server's log. The pass frees its Vulkan objects at Reset, ResetEx, device destroy and when its depth texture is destroyed. Counters (passes, rays, dispatch time by device timestamps, faults) sit in a 64-byte shared block and in the server's log as a [GiPixel] line. Test: test-gi-pixel.cmd (test_gi_pixel_device). The server compiles gi_pixel_pass.h, gi_pixel_block.h and pixel_shadow.comp, which native/remix-bridge/build.cmd copies in from the repository (native/remix-bridge/gi, tools/gi_server_test).
Applies after 0018 (with the scene submit and texel solver of R-04).
